IMHO this 3.0 is too difficult. 

For example, can anyone demonstrate a suitable level of difficulty by
playing 10 games and getting past level 10 at least 5 times? I mean, I
don't play Nethack because I enjoy getting killed, but for the
challence. If, however, I always get killed at DLevel 7 at the latest no
matter what I do, I can not see the challence anywhere.

I have played umpteen games, and only once I managed to level 7.

Pet Peeves:
-----------

1. Famine in Netland.  There is too little food at least in the first
few levels of the dungeon. I manage by resorting to the gods, but my pet
invariably starves to death. The few times I have found a stethoscope,
and been able to investigate, it has seemed my pet will never grow to be
a big dog/housecat. The pet's HP gets lower and lower without adequate
nourishment. The probability for finding food and for killed monsters
leaving a corpse should be higher. 

2.  Monsters not eating.  Why is it, that me and my pet seem to be the
only ones in the dungeon that have a habit of eating? I have been
trapped between monsters with a ring of regeneration and plenty of food,
but waiting until the monsters get fed up or starve newer works.  On
occasion, I have escaped a particularly vicious monster to another
Dlevel, only to find, when I return 2000 turns later, the ravenous beast
still waiting for me. 

3. Monsters too bloody big. Even in Dlevels 3 .. 5 there appear monsters
that are difficult to beat for a HP:50 EXP:6 character. And, when they
come in hordes, I ran out of magical and other tricks and get killed.

4. Monsters out of nowhere. I don't like this bit about monsters
materializing from thin air in the same room I am in, waiting for my HP
getting back to par. I have been trapped into a corner because of this.
If monsters materialize out of nowhere, at least make them appear one by
one so that it is possible to get out of the room. 

5.  Killer bee too small to hit.  Why do I keep on missing killer bees?
I have been a EXP:5 samurai, and missed a killer bee 200 turns in
sequence.  I was trapped in a corridor between two killer bees and had a
ring of regeneration and plenty of food.  I kept hitting the bees,
throwing things at them, putting them to sleep and so on.  Missed all
the time.  Eventually the other monster who were throwing things at me
got the bees killed.  Should bees be hit with a special weapon 
(fly swatter? :-)) or how are they to be dealt with. 

6. Pets and pits. How to prevent my pet from getting killed by falling
to a pit I have discovered?

7. Altars, anyone? Are there altars in version 3.0e? I haven{t seen any
of lawful since I patched the original version (I play lawful
characters). There are not too many shops either. Perhaps the
probability of a new Dlevel having a shop should increase for every
Dlevel discovered without a shop, and similarly for altars.

Summary: I dont't mind the game beeing hard, 2.3 was quite easy to win
if you knew the ropes. Winning 3.0 seems impropable even if I use all
the tricks I know. 


